# Licensing

`displaceR` is released under the GPL-2, matching upstream DISPLACE.

## Why GPL-2 and not something more permissive

`install_displace()` downloads and installs binaries built from the DISPLACE
sources (https://github.com/frabas/DISPLACE_GUI), which are GPL-2.0. Those
binaries are published as release assets of this repository, so this repository
distributes GPL-2 covered work and must be GPL-2 compatible.

## Corresponding source

GPL-2 section 3 requires that the corresponding source accompany the binary.
For every binary asset this repository publishes, the corresponding source is:

- the upstream commit SHA recorded in `inst/manifest.json` under
  `upstream_sha`, in the repository `https://github.com/frabas/DISPLACE_GUI`;
- the exact build recipe in `tools/build-displace.sh` and
  `.github/workflows/build-displace.yml` at the commit that produced the asset.

Both are recorded in the release notes of every build. The build is reproducible
from those two pieces alone.

## Third-party runtime components in the tarball

The published tarball contains:

| File | Origin | License |
|---|---|---|
| `displace` | DISPLACE_GUI | GPL-2.0 |
| `libcommons.so` | DISPLACE_GUI | GPL-2.0 |
| `libformats.so` | DISPLACE_GUI | GPL-2.0 |
| `libmsqlitecpp.so.1` | https://github.com/studiofuga/mSqliteCpp | see upstream |

Everything else the binary links against (Boost, GeographicLib, sqlite3,
libstdc++, libc) is a stock system library and is not redistributed.

